# UrbanOS triage model.
#
# A LoRA adapter over the base llama3.1:8b that Ollama already serves, rather
# than a merged copy of it: the adapter is ~160MB against the base's 4.9GB, and
# the base stays byte-identical so the NARRATION path (/api/chat) is untouched.
# That separation is deliberate -- base llama3.1:8b was verified to narrate the
# precomputed report figures correctly, and only classification needed work.
#
# Build:  python finetune/export_gguf.py
#   or:   ollama create urbanos-triage -f finetune/Modelfile
# Use:    OLLAMA_TRIAGE_MODEL=urbanos-triage   (llm.py reads this separately
#         from OLLAMA_CHAT_MODEL for exactly this reason)

FROM llama3.1:8b
ADAPTER ./adapter/urbanos-triage-lora-f16.gguf

# Classification, not prose. Temperature 0 and no top-k/top-p sampling: a
# citizen's complaint must route to the same department every time it is
# submitted, and a sampled enum is a coin flip over departments.
PARAMETER temperature 0
PARAMETER top_p 1
PARAMETER top_k 1
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0

# Triage prompt plus schema fits well inside this; the caller also sets num_ctx.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

SYSTEM """You are the UrbanOS triage classifier for Lucknow municipal grievances. You return one JSON object matching the required schema and nothing else. Routing follows Lucknow's departments: electricity and street lighting to LESA, water, sewage and drainage to Jal Sansthan, unauthorised building and encroachment to LDA, highways to PWD, and everything else to Nagar Nigam. semantic_tag is a canonical snake_case topic tag, identical for every report of the same real-world issue."""
